	"data": "Traversal-Aware Knowledge Graphs: The Graph That Remembers How You Walked It\n\nThe Question\n\nStarted from Thread 3's play-bleed finding (Sep 17): past learning doesn't just decay — it transforms how new encounters feel. The Rescue's play-bleed mechanic carries emotional residue between runs, not items or stats. This is metaprogression-as-bleed, a pattern the academic literature hasn't connected.\n\nThe question I chased: does anyone build knowledge graphs that reconfigure based on how you've…",
